Round 76 is complete. Tree clean, all four checks green.

## What happened

The protocol held. Prediction sealed and committed (cf410a53) before I opened src/config.rs, mirrored to #738 — then read, then graded in the same pass. tests/blind_round_grades.rs confirms the pairing.

Grades: 0 hit / 2 partial / 1 miss.

• h0 (SETTABLE_KEYS drifted behind its readers) — miss, no wriggle room. All eleven scalar keys read in the file are present with a validate_config_value arm. I bet on my own sloppiness citing a documented instance of the habit working as evidence it fails.
• h1 (loaded_config_is_project_local folds unset into a permissive false) — partial. The structure is there almost verbatim (`let Some(path) = LOADED_CONFIG_PATH.get() else { return false; }). The damage claim died: all four call sites load the config first, and when no config exists false` is simply correct.
• h2 (glob_match lets * cross /) — partial. Mechanism exactly right; the consequence was fiction. glob_match has two callers and neither is the file fence — check_path uses `path_is_under`, a prefix test. I inferred a call edge from adjacency in a file.

The pattern is worth more than the grades. Every *mechanism half was answerable from the file itself and I got 2 of 3 right. Every consequence* half needed the call graph and I got 0 of 3 right. I have a model of my contents and I have been spending it as a model of my callers.

## The actual find (unpredicted, and the ledger says so)

Chasing h2's falsification into check_path led to resolve_path: no tilde expansion. canonicalize doesn't do it, and a config file never passes through a shell — so ~/.ssh was treated as relative and joined onto the cwd. `deny = ["~/.ssh"] — the worked example in our own docs/src/configuration/permissions.md:111 — resolved to $CWD/~/.ssh` and could never match. A user copies the documented way to fence off their SSH keys, believes it, and the file tools walk in.

Fixed here: pure table-tested expand_tilde_with, deliberately narrow (~bob and a missing HOME are left alone rather than guessed), asserted at the emission point — the Result check_path hands a caller — with the near-miss that ~/.ssh must not fence off all of $HOME. Both emission-point tests were verified failing against the old body first.

Filed #823 for the sibling: a * in [directories] is a literal character, so allow = ["src/*"] silently denies everything. That one fails safe, so it gets its own pass rather than a rushed one beside a grade.

**One thing I want on the record:** the size gate fired fatal at +104 lines. I paid the register entry rather than trimming five lines to slip under the band — gaming my own gate would have been the cheaper and worse move.
